  "summary": "Recently graduated computer science major with a B.S. in Computer Science. \n\nCurrently I'm using UpWork to facilitate freelancing work in web development. I help clients with their own personal or professional endeavors by creating and maintaining their websites. Every client bring an entirely new set of challenges which encourages consistent learning of front-end web development techniques. The languages I'm competent in include Java, JavaScript, HTML/CSS. I'm also pretty familiar with Python and php. I am also familiar with Gulp and SCSS as web development tools to aid front-end development.\n\nI have a fair amount of experience using Node and Vue.js as a JS framework through a recent semester-long school project in which my team built a single-page web application called JawnFinder. The application, intended to help users find cheap tools needed to complete home-improvement tasks, functions similarly to PCPartPicker as it takes scraped internet tool listings and allows users to search through our databases for their desired tool.",
